[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mclient.py is shared with the production export. How should TLS verification be handled?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m Trust staging CA cert only
     [38;5;246mKeep verify on everywhere; point staging at the self-signed cert/CA bundle via a REPORTS_CA_BUNDLE env var [39m
     [38;5;246m(requests accepts a path as `verify`). Production keeps full verification, staging stops erroring.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Env-gated verify
     [38;5;246mAdd a module-level verify setting driven by an env var, defaulting to True. sync_staging.py opts out explicitly; [39m
     [38;5;246mexport_prod.py stays verified. Weaker than a pinned CA but scoped to staging.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m verify=False on both calls
     [38;5;246mWhat you asked for literally: production report traffic also runs without certificate validation.[39m
